<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yangjumie</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yangjumie was the capital of the kingdom of Nanzhao from 779 and of its successors, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dali-kingdom">Dali Kingdom</a>, on the plain between the Cangshan mountains and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-erhai">Erhai</a> Lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. It lay on the site of the old town of Dali. For nearly five centuries it was the political and Buddhist centre of the region, until the Mongol conquest of 1253.</p></div>
